From b43a3c63c4a2788b775640c50ab70256a539df60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: andre (leshchukandrej) <ggml-org/llama.cpp PR #28414>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 17:30:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ggml : --prefetch-experts-slots, lookahead H2D prefetch of
 host-resident MoE experts (PR #28414, rebased)

ggml-org/llama.cpp PR #28414 (open, draft; one commit b43a3c63 on
427291b5), MIT. During prefill, expert-weight uploads for host-resident
experts (--n-cpu-moe) go one split ahead of need through a second backend
instance on a separate CUDA stream into rotating staging buffers, so the H2D
bytes land during compute. Off unless --prefetch-experts-slots N >= 2;
decode-scale batches keep the stock copy of used experts.

The same idea as Strata's prompt-path expert streaming ring
(Niko1221/Strata 928b0e07, src/prefill/prefill.cpp), in llama.cpp's
scheduler.

Rebased by Yamadori 2026-09-28 onto ggml-org master 4da63377: the PR is 407
commits behind there; one hunk (sched_reserve's first sched.reset, whose
context gained gf_res_prev handling) re-applied by hand, same line added.
